# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TG-Capital Local — Environment Configuration
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your own values:
#   cp .env.example .env
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Schwab API Credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get these from https://developer.schwab.com → My Apps → your app
# App Key    → SCHWAB_CLIENT_ID
# App Secret → SCHWAB_CLIENT_SECRET
SCHWAB_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_SCHWAB_APP_KEY_HERE
SCHWAB_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR_SCHWAB_APP_SECRET_HERE

# ── Ollama (AI) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where Ollama is running. If Ollama is on the same machine as Docker, leave as-is.
# If Ollama is on a different machine, change to http://<ip>:11434
OLLAMA_HOST=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# ── AI Models (optional overrides) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Chat model — pull first: ollama pull 0xroyce/plutus
CHAT_MODEL=0xroyce/plutus

# Retried once, automatically, if CHAT_MODEL errors or crashes mid-request (see
# ollamaChatWithFallback in server.js). Requires OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1 on the
# Ollama service so the primary is evicted from VRAM before the fallback loads —
# otherwise two large models can end up resident at once and crash the host.
# CHAT_MODEL_FALLBACK=qwen3-vl-32b-tgcapital

# Sampling temperature for the main chat loop (0-1). Lower = more consistent,
# less prone to hedging/fabricating numbers that should come straight from a
# tool result. Default 0.25 if unset.
CHAT_TEMPERATURE=0.25

# Embedding model — auto-detected. Uncomment to force a specific one:
# ollama pull mxbai-embed-large
# EMBED_MODEL=mxbai-embed-large

# ── Web Search — Perplexity (recommended) ────────────────────────────────────
# Perplexity Sonar gives real-time web search with citations. Best quality.
# Get your key at https://www.perplexity.ai → Settings → API
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=YOUR_PERPLEXITY_API_KEY_HERE

# ── Web Search — Ollama (optional fallback) ───────────────────────────────────
# Ollama's own web search API. Used alongside Perplexity when both keys are set.
# Get your key at https://ollama.com → Account → API Keys
OLLAMA_API_KEY=YOUR_OLLAMA_API_KEY_HERE

# ── Sector Classification — Finnhub (Performance Coach tab + company profile) ─
# Used to classify tickers by sector for the Performance Coach dashboard's
# sector breakdown chart, and to show a brief company-profile line (name,
# industry, exchange, market cap) on the Proactive Scout trade-idea canvas.
# Free tier is plenty (sector refreshed at most every 30 days per ticker).
# Get a free key at https://finnhub.io/
FINNHUB_API_KEY=YOUR_FINNHUB_API_KEY_HERE

# ── Proactive Scout — SEC filing ingest ───────────────────────────────────────
# Bearer token required by POST /api/v1/ingest (what local/sec_scraper.py posts to,
# whether run manually, via cron, or via the .github/workflows/sec-scraper.yml
# GitHub Action). Generate one yourself, e.g.: openssl rand -hex 32
# Also set this as a GitHub Actions secret of the same name if using the workflow.
SCOUT_INGEST_TOKEN=YOUR_RANDOM_TOKEN_HERE

# Small local model used by the Contradiction Engine ("Truth Check" on /scout) to
# compare a filing's own Risk Factors vs MD&A tone, and against retail sentiment.
# Only needs JSON-mode completion, not tool-calling — defaults to gemma4:e2b if unset.
# See local/FinanceLlama.Modelfile for a worked example of building a larger-context
# variant of a finance-tuned model instead.
# CONTRADICTION_MODEL=gemma4:e2b

# Same fallback behavior as CHAT_MODEL_FALLBACK above, for the Contradiction Engine.
# CONTRADICTION_MODEL_FALLBACK=qwen3-vl-32b-tgcapital

# SEC asks for an identifying User-Agent on requests to sec.gov/data.sec.gov.
# Used by both local/sec_scraper.py and the server's own inline SEC fetch.
# SEC_USER_AGENT=YourApp/1.0 you@example.com

# ── 8-K Discovery Alerts — Gmail (optional; see local/sec-scraper-README.md) ─
# Server-side OAuth (separate from the main app's browser-only Drive integration) —
# needs its own Client Secret and a one-time Google Cloud Console setup. Without these
# set, 8-K discovery/analysis still runs; only alert-sending is skipped.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID_HERE
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET_HERE
# GMAIL_SEND_TO=you@example.com

# Discord: consolidated 8-K alerts also post here (Discord server -> channel ->
# Edit Channel -> Integrations -> Webhooks -> New Webhook -> Copy URL). Optional —
# without this set, alert-sending just skips Discord and still emails as before.
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/YOUR_ID/YOUR_TOKEN
